// An active open: our SYN with the MSS and the timestamps, the peer's SYN-ACK, our ACK at the flush, which echoes
// the peer's value. connect returns at once, as a non-blocking connect does; the ACK is deferred so a commit could
// ride it.
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 fcntl(3, F_SETFL, O_RDWR|O_NONBLOCK) = 0
+0 connect(3, ..., ...) = -1 EINPROGRESS (Operation now in progress)
+0 > S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 0>
+0 < S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 > . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
